---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: project.run(args)
---
Search, list and read past Claude Code sessions, to bring context from earlier conversations into the current one.

SCOPE
  By default only sessions started in exactly the current directory are listed, read and searched. Subdirectories and other projects need --all. Every project is indexed either way, and claudegrep keeps its own compressed copy of every transcript, so sessions stay readable after Claude Code deletes old transcripts (cleanupPeriodDays, 30 days by default).

WORKFLOW
  claudegrep "how did we fix the token refresh"   find sessions and the places that match
  claudegrep read <id> --outline                  one line per turn: the session's table of contents
  claudegrep read <id> --from 12.0                read from turn 12; output is paged, the end names the next --from
  claudegrep read <id> --from 12.0 --deep         the same with tool calls, tool results and thinking

POSITIONS
  TURN.PART, e.g. 12.3. A turn is one user message, one Claude reply (everything Claude did until the next user message) or one subagent report. Long turns are split into parts. Search results print the exact position of each match, ready for `read --from`. A --deep page that stops inside a reply names the place as TURN:BLOCK, e.g. 12:7. A block is one message, thinking block or tool call of the reply.

PAGES
  read prints one page of at most --budget characters (setting: budget) and ends with the command that prints the next one. --budget N changes the size for one call, and --budget 0 prints everything at once.

TIME
  --since and --until take a date (2026-10-14) or an age (30m, 6h, 2d, 1w, 3mo) and keep the sessions that were active in that window. A session's time comes from its transcript entries.

NOTES
  Inside Claude Code, search skips the calling session (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID). Settings live in the database: claudegrep config.

Usage: claudegrep [OPTIONS] [QUERY]... [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list    List sessions, most recent first
  read    Read a session as markdown, paged
  search  Search (the default when a query is given)
  index   Index every project now (search does this on its own)
  status  Show what is indexed and archived
  forget  Remove an archived session from claudegrep
  config  Show or change settings
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [QUERY]...
          What to search for (same as `claudegrep search <query>`)

Options:
  -n, --limit <LIMIT>
          Number of matching chunks to show [config: limit]

  -B, --before <N>
          Also show the N chunks before each match, from the same session

  -A, --after <N>
          Also show the N chunks after each match, from the same session

  -C, --context <N>
          Also show N chunks before and after each match

      --all
          Use every project's sessions, not only those started in the current directory

      --since <WHEN>
          Only sessions active since WHEN: a date (2026-10-14) or an age (30m, 6h, 2d, 1w, 3mo)

      --until <WHEN>
          Only sessions active until WHEN: a date (whole day included) or an age

      --db <FILE>
          Database with the index, the transcript archive and the settings
          
          [env: CLAUDEGREP_DB=[ROOT]/db.sqlite]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
